# Guardrail config (protected). OWASP ZAP baseline rules, used by ci/dast.sh (docs/security/owasp.md).
# Format: <rule id><TAB><IGNORE|INFO|WARN|FAIL><TAB>(<name>) — any rule not listed defaults to WARN,
# and warnings fail the scan too. IGNORE only with a reason, never to make a real finding go away.
10020	FAIL	(Missing Anti-clickjacking Header)
10021	FAIL	(X-Content-Type-Options Header Missing)
10038	FAIL	(Content Security Policy Header Not Set)
10036	FAIL	(Server Leaks Version Information via "Server" HTTP Response Header Field)
10037	FAIL	(Server Leaks Information via "X-Powered-By" HTTP Response Header Field(s))
# The API sends Cache-Control: no-store on purpose (responses may contain export data).
10049	IGNORE	(Non-Storable Content)
# Informational only: suggests the Ajax spider for JavaScript apps; the UI flows are covered by Playwright.
10109	IGNORE	(Modern Web Application)
{%- if frontend == 'ssr' %}
# Server-rendered UI only: an informational alert (not a finding) that the CSRF cookie looks like session handling.
# Reported, not ignored; the cookie's flags are checked by the cookie rules (10010, 10011, 10054) and by tests.
10112	INFO	(Session Management Response Identified)
{%- endif %}
{%- if frontend == 'react-native' %}
# React Native web bundle only: minified library code contains large numbers that look like Unix timestamps.
10096	IGNORE	(Timestamp Disclosure - Unix)
# React Native web bundle only: library code references eval-like functions; the CSP has no 'unsafe-eval', so they
# cannot run, and the Playwright suite proves the app works under that CSP.
10110	IGNORE	(Dangerous JS Functions)
{%- endif %}
